 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 28121,
   "ANSWER": "<ul>\n\t<li data-end=\"1562\" data-start=\"1427\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1447\" data-start=\"1430\"><strong data-end=\"1445\" data-start=\"1430\">Definition:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1562\" data-start=\"1451\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1506\" data-start=\"1451\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1506\" data-start=\"1453\">MMIO: I/O devices are accessed as memory locations.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1562\" data-start=\"1510\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1562\" data-start=\"1512\">PMIO: I/O devices have a separate address space.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1708\" data-start=\"1564\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1582\" data-start=\"1567\"><strong data-end=\"1580\" data-start=\"1567\">Examples:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1708\" data-start=\"1586\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1659\" data-start=\"1586\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1659\" data-start=\"1588\">MMIO: <code data-end=\"1615\" data-start=\"1594\">LDR R1, [R0, #0x10]</code> (Access device at address offset <code data-end=\"1655\" data-start=\"1649\">0x10</code>).</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1708\" data-start=\"1663\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1708\" data-start=\"1665\">PMIO: Uses <code data-end=\"1680\" data-start=\"1676\">IN</code>/<code data-end=\"1686\" data-start=\"1681\">OUT</code> instructions (x86).</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1861\" data-start=\"1710\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1738\" data-start=\"1713\"><strong data-end=\"1736\" data-start=\"1713\">Advantages of MMIO:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1861\" data-start=\"1742\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1783\" data-start=\"1742\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1783\" data-start=\"1744\">Uniform addressing simplifies design.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1829\" data-start=\"1787\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1829\" data-start=\"1789\">Uses existing LOAD/STORE instructions.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1861\" data-start=\"1833\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1861\" data-start=\"1835\">Larger addressing space.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1965\" data-start=\"1863\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1894\" data-start=\"1866\"><strong data-end=\"1892\" data-start=\"1866\">Disadvantages of MMIO:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1965\" data-start=\"1898\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1932\" data-start=\"1898\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1932\" data-start=\"1900\">Consumes memory address space.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1965\" data-start=\"1936\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1965\" data-start=\"1938\">Potential bus contention.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2071\" data-start=\"1967\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1995\" data-start=\"1970\"><strong data-end=\"1993\" data-start=\"1970\">Advantages of PMIO:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"2071\" data-start=\"1999\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"2034\" data-start=\"1999\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"2034\" data-start=\"2001\">Separate address space for I/O.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"2071\" data-start=\"2038\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"2071\" data-start=\"2040\">Reduces memory address usage.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2175\" data-start=\"2073\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2104\" data-start=\"2076\"><strong data-end=\"2102\" data-start=\"2076\">Disadvantages of PMIO:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"2175\" data-start=\"2108\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"2142\" data-start=\"2108\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"2142\" data-start=\"2110\">Requires special instructions.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"2175\" data-start=\"2146\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"2175\" data-start=\"2148\">More complex programming.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2284\" data-start=\"2177\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2196\" data-start=\"2180\"><strong data-end=\"2194\" data-start=\"2180\">Use Cases:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"2284\" data-start=\"2200\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"2238\" data-start=\"2200\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"2238\" data-start=\"2202\">MMIO: Embedded RISC systems (ARM).</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"2284\" data-start=\"2242\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"2284\" data-start=\"2244\">PMIO: Legacy CISC architectures (x86).</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 4,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO2"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>Discuss <strong data-end=\"1212\" data-start=\"1184\">Memory-Mapped I/O (MMIO)</strong> vs <strong data-end=\"1242\" data-start=\"1216\">Port-Mapped I/O (PMIO)</strong> in embedded systems. Explain their differences, advantages, disadvantages, and provide examples with ARM instructions.</p>\n",
